From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 00:16:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 437/488] Spec decode: verified tokens carry their
 logprob_token_ids

A request's logprob_token_ids name the tokens whose logprobs it gets for
every generated token; the OpenAI APIs send them with logprobs unset. The
V2 runner's sampler returns them, but with speculative decoding only the
token of a step without drafts goes through it. Every verified token went
through the rejection sampler, which sized its logprobs from
sampling_states (the logprobs parameter alone) and never passed the
requests' ids to compute_topk_scores; a greedy batch that wanted only
custom ids also took greedy verification, which returns no logprobs. So
verified tokens came back without logprobs, or with the top logprobs of
a neighbour's request instead of the ids, and a chat completion with
logprob_token_ids got fewer logprob entries than tokens: IndexError in
_create_chat_logprobs, HTTP 500. With sink rejection the first token's
row was dropped as well, since the step that verifies it had none.

The rejection sampler now takes the sampler's logprobs dimensions (top
logprobs and per-request ids) and scores each logits row as the sampler
does, with the request-state index of each row; it also scores the sink
alternates and clamps dead rows whenever any request wants logprobs.
Greedy verification is taken only when no request wants logprobs,
logprob_token_ids included. The batch-sharded gather takes the ids'
columns for verification steps too, so get_logprobs_dims no longer has an
include_token_ids switch. Requests without logprobs are unchanged: their
steps take the same paths as before.

boundary_checkpoint.py's slot constants follow watermark.py's HAS_TRITON
guard, so the V2 runner's sampler, rejection sampler and model runner
import without Triton (CPU tests). With Triton they are unchanged.

Tests: tests/v1/worker/test_gpu_verified_logprob_token_ids.py runs the
real sampling state and rejection sampler on the host (host tensors for
the device buffers, torch references for the Triton launches it
reaches): every verified token carries its request's ids' logprobs in
its row's distribution, alone and beside a top-logprobs request and one
without logprobs, in one verification chunk or several and with adaptive
verification, in every logprobs mode; the sink alternates are scored for
an ids-only batch; greedy verification is refused when any request wants
ids. All but the two greedy cases without ids fail without the change.
The scripted worker of test_sink_draft_zero.py returns rows with the
ids, and the scheduler, the output processor and _create_chat_logprobs
give one entry per token, with the ids scored in the draw that chose
each token, a rejected draft zero's replacement included (this part
passes before the change too).
